---
const SIGNUP_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in';
---

<section class="py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Reverse DCF</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Know the return<br />
          <em class="font-semibold not-italic">today's price leaves you</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Reverse DCF starts from the price. Enter the earnings per share and Margin divides the
          price by it for the PE you would be buying at. Add the holding period you have in mind, the PE you
          expect to sell at and the earnings growth you believe in, and Margin works out the
          yearly return you would earn buying at that price.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
          State the growth as a yearly rate, or as the EPS or profit you expect at the end of the
          period, and Margin converts between them. When the return falls short of what you want
          from the stock, the price already asks for more growth than you are prepared to assume.
        </p>
        <a
          href={SIGNUP_URL}
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors group"
        >
          Try Reverse DCF
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="relative rounded-xl border border-border bg-navy-800/40 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold-400/30 to-transparent"></div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-xs text-muted tracking-widest uppercase mb-6">Reverse DCF Calculator</p>
            <div class="space-y-3 mb-6">
              {[
                { label: 'Holding period', value: '5 yrs', sub: 'How long you intend to hold' },
                { label: 'Current PE', value: '30', sub: "Today's price over the EPS you enter" },
                { label: 'Exit PE', value: '25', sub: 'What you expect to sell at' },
                { label: 'EPS growth', value: '14%', sub: 'A year, or the EPS or profit you expect in year five' },
              ].map((row) => (
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-3 border-b border-border/50">
                  <div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink">{row.label}</p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted">{row.sub}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="font-display text-lg text-cream">{row.value}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/60 border border-gold-400/20 p-5">
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-1">Annualised return</p>
              <p class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-gold-400">10.0%</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2">A year, for the five years you hold it, if the growth and exit PE hold</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-muted">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400"></span>
              Short of the 15% you want from the stock
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
